<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mia Mottley</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1965">1965</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mia Mottley is a Barbadian lawyer and politician who became the first woman prime minister of Barbados in May 2018, when her <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbados-labour-party">Barbados Labour Party</a> won every seat in parliament. Her government oversaw the country's transition to a parliamentary republic in November 2021, and she has become an international voice on climate change and debt through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bridgetown-initiative">Bridgetown Initiative</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mia-mottley.jpg" alt="Mia Mottley" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Foreign, Commonwealth &amp; Development Office · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Foreign_Secretary_Yvette_Cooper_meets_with_Barbados_Prime_Minister_-_5535661749_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
